Demonstration closes the streets of Helsinki city centre
The demonstration on Friday will close the streets of the centre of Helsinki.
According to the police, the streets leading to the Railway Square are closed from the cars around 9:30–14 a.m.
Cars will not be allowed towards Kaivokatu, Postikatu or Töölönlahdenkatu in the direction of the railway station.
From Unioninkatu to Hakaniemi, traffic is directed to Unioninkatu at the Kaisaniemi roundabout.
According to the police, the closing time depends on the number involved in the demonstration.
Only emergency vehicles will be allowed into the area.
Metro and tram drivers throughout Friday's demonstration
Metro and tram drivers will take part in Friday's demonstration from the beginning of morning traffic to the end of night traffic.
Trax and metro personnel's association told STT about the matter in the evening.
The majority of Alkot closes for two hours, also mail closed
