Three-in-a-finals agree that Sam Wood is the perfect guy, but whose does he choose?
"The secret has been revealed?"
Lana Jeavons-Fellows, Sarah Mackay and Snezana Markoski may have accidentally revealed who would win The Bachelor.
That woman's identity has been kept extremely secret, with which Sam Wood ends up together at The Bachelor.
Three of the remaining girls don't really slick who got the last rose.
However, when we were discussing with Sarah Mackay, Snezana Markoski and Lana Jeavons-Fellows the day before three of them turned out to be two, they could inadvertently give a clue to the victor's identity.
Sam Wood's lips have been sealed before Thursday's final
All three women threw themselves poetically into how Wood is the perfect man, mentioning his sense of humour, ambition, family value and positivity as the reasons why they would want to be his partner.
However, when they were asked, “If Wood’s last rose isn’t for you, who is it supposed to go to?”, their responses might have provided a revelation about who won the bachelor’s heart.
Both Jeavons-Fellows and Markoski quickly mentioned Mackay as the best option for Wood after themselves.
Sarah Mackay and Sam Wood have been uncomplicated since day one.
“From the moment I walked into the house (Sarahi’s) energies and Sam’s energies felt quite compatible, and that idea was on my mind throughout the series,” Jeavons-Fellows said.
‘Sarah is really down-to-earthy, it’s fun to be with him,’ Markoski added.
I've seen them together and there's chemistry between them.
They seem to be comfortable and relaxed together.
Sarah Mackay thinks she and Sam Wood would be a good partner.
Mackay said last week's home visits made him realize that Wood could be “the one.”
“When I saw him with my friends and my family, I realized that it’s obviously not just a game – I’m now with all my heart involved in this,” he said.
When asked who Wood should choose if he didn't, Mackay was mysterious.
‘I don’t know if I can say,’ he said.
I like the remaining girls just as much, so it's a draw between Snezana and Lana.
The Bachelor will be broadcast Wednesday at 19:30 on Ten.
