Unemployment among Scots will remain the same as the UK's integer grows
UNEMPLOYMENTMENT in Scotland remained at 164 000 people between May and July, at the same time, while unemployment throughout the United Kingdom rose by a total of 1,82 million persons.
Scotland's unemployment figure of 5.9 per cent is higher than the UK's 5.5 per cent, according to the National Bureau of Statistics (ONS).
At the same time, unemployment in Scotland fell by 12 000 people over a three-month period, and the number of employed persons is now 2 612 000.
