If Glossip dies, he believes that publicity will help a trend that opposes the death penalty.
Huffington Port reporter Kim Bellware is by my side.
If you want to know more about the article, you can listen to the podcasts I've made.
I won't go through all the details here again.
I'm unable to say with certainty that Richard Glossip is innocent.
In any case, his actions after the murder of Barry Van Treese would in any case make him culprit in aiding.
But I think there's a very strong possibility that he hasn't committed murder.
I'm sure there wasn't enough evidence justifiing the death penalty.
I think it's wrong to execute him.
And that's the point of view I'm looking at him dying from.
I can't say I'm completely neutral.
There will be other journalists who will take care of it.
You'll give me a description of what it's like to look at when the man I like dies unnecessarily.
