Norris (2-2, 4.43 ERA) will take on Minnesota's right-handed pitcher Ervin Santana (5-4, 4.73 ERA).
Xi urges opening up the economy to the wider world
“The economy needs to open up more to the outside world to promote growth,” President Xi Jinping told a group to guide the reform.
“China should commit to attracting foreign funding and expertise and developing a transparency policy,” he said, addressing the 16th meeting of the leading group to deepen global reform.
At the same time as reforms are being pushed forward, we are pushing for more new movement and vitality, and creating new space for economic growth, Xi said.
The management team approved a series of guidelines, including a negative list of restrictions on market access, a laxisation of border control principles, the call for state-owned companies to seize private capital, and a revision of the resident registration system.
According to the opinion, a negative list will be created to name the sectors and companies that are not allowed to invest.
The system will be gradually tested and upgraded through trial programmes.
The change will be significant, as it will play a greater role in the allocation of resources to the market, ensure a law-based business environment and make the market more transparent, the statement said.
The government will also loosen its control over the power it distributes to companies, thus ensuring that companies decide for themselves how to manage their business.
It was also said that China will allow border regions to explore new cross-border economic cooperation models and new mechanisms for the development of regional growth.
In order to open state-controlled sectors, more sectors will be opened up to private financiers.
“The government will not change its policy on foreign investment and will protect the legal interests of foreign-funded companies as well as provide them with better services,” the statement said.
In addition, the application process for foreign permanent resident permits, ‘green cards’, is facilitated by optimizing the requirements and streamlining the application process.
The meeting also discussed guaranteeing the professional rights of lawyers and supporting professional referees and prosecutors.
The meeting was also attended by Prime Minister Li Keqiang, as well as senior leaders Liu Yunshan and Zhang Gaoli.
